{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44246172",
      "title": "Fetching Data with RSCs",
      "sourceHash": "01b7b13974ae246a682f0b3600ddbcf17cca88ae985e26b2023bb65d339d20f9",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 5.31,
          "en": "So, now we had an in-depth look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.31,
          "end": 7.98,
          "en": "at server components, client components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.98,
          "end": 10.65,
          "en": "and how we can combine them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.65,
          "end": 14.04,
          "en": "Next, I want to explore data fetching with you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.04,
          "end": 17.1,
          "en": "because when using server components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.1,
          "end": 19.08,
          "en": "you have some new options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.08,
          "end": 22.473,
          "en": "when it comes to fetching data in your components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.31,
          "end": 27.54,
          "en": "And therefore, attached you'll find two new files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.54,
          "end": 31.44,
          "en": "The first one is a file named dummy-db.json,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.44,
          "end": 34.263,
          "en": "which you should add in your root project folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.31,
          "end": 37.77,
          "en": "That's a file that contains some dummy data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.77,
          "end": 41.853,
          "en": "and kind of simulates a database here, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.69,
          "end": 47.69,
          "en": "And then attached you'll find a DataFetchingDemo.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.79,
          "end": 51.9,
          "en": "which you should also paste into your components folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.9,
          "end": 55.848,
          "en": "And this DataFetchingDemo.js file contains",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.848,
          "end": 59.52,
          "en": "a server component as you can tell by the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.52,
          "end": 62.85,
          "en": "that there is no use client directive at the top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.85,
          "end": 65.94,
          "en": "and that we have the async keyword here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.94,
          "end": 69,
          "en": "And I did add the async keyword here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 69,
          "end": 73.98,
          "en": "because this component now actually also contains some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 73.98,
          "end": 76.8,
          "en": "that does fetch some data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.8,
          "end": 80.55,
          "en": "It contains some Node.js code for opening a file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 80.55,
          "end": 82.41,
          "en": "and reading the file content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.41,
          "end": 85.5,
          "en": "and for then loading data from that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.5,
          "end": 88.28999999999999,
          "en": "And then that data, these users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 88.28999999999999,
          "end": 92.7,
          "en": "are output in the JSX code of this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.7,
          "end": 96.27000000000001,
          "en": "And in normal components, in client components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 96.27000000000001,
          "end": 100.71000000000001,
          "en": "and components as you would add them to Vite-based projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 100.71000000000001,
          "end": 104.22,
          "en": "for example, this would not work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 104.22,
          "end": 108.27000000000001,
          "en": "There, you can't put Node.js code into your components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 108.27000000000001,
          "end": 110.158,
          "en": "and you can't use async await",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 110.158,
          "end": 113.07,
          "en": "because they're executed in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 113.07,
          "end": 116.43,
          "en": "And whilst the browser does indeed support async await,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 116.43,
          "end": 119.82300000000001,
          "en": "React doesn't support it for client components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 120.84,
          "end": 125.58,
          "en": "But when we have server components, this entire code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 125.58,
          "end": 128.31,
          "en": "as you learned, executes on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 128.31,
          "end": 131.46,
          "en": "So in a Node.js environment for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 131.46,
          "end": 135.3,
          "en": "and if that's the case, we can write Node.js code in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 135.3,
          "end": 139.23,
          "en": "and this code will never execute on the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 139.23,
          "end": 143.97,
          "en": "And therefore, React server components vastly simplify",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 143.97,
          "end": 147.24,
          "en": "the process of fetching data in components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 147.24,
          "end": 150.93,
          "en": "because instead of using useEffect to wrap code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 150.93,
          "end": 153.84,
          "en": "that fetches data from a separate backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 153.84,
          "end": 156.72,
          "en": "the code for loading the data is included",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 156.72,
          "end": 158.73,
          "en": "right in the component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 158.73,
          "end": 160.62,
          "en": "And this is then executed on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 160.62,
          "end": 162.78,
          "en": "and the finished HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 162.78,
          "end": 166.53,
          "en": "that includes the fetch data is then sent back to the client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 166.53,
          "end": 168.93,
          "en": "and is displayed there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.93,
          "end": 173.28,
          "en": "And therefore here what we can do with that file added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 173.28,
          "end": 177.6,
          "en": "we can go to the page.js file and get rid of the ClientDemo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 177.6,
          "end": 180.33,
          "en": "and RSCDemo components here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 180.33,
          "end": 184.77,
          "en": "and instead output this DataFetchingDemo component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 184.77,
          "end": 187.8,
          "en": "and remove these unused imports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 187.8,
          "end": 189.49099999999999,
          "en": "And if you do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 189.49099999999999,
          "end": 192.84,
          "en": "and you then go back to your website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 192.84,
          "end": 195.57,
          "en": "to this development server preview here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 195.57,
          "end": 198.15,
          "en": "you see this component being rendered here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 198.15,
          "end": 201.003,
          "en": "and you see the loaded data being rendered here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 202.11,
          "end": 205.59,
          "en": "And that now was all rendered on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 205.59,
          "end": 208.803,
          "en": "or not on the client, to put it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 209.79,
          "end": 212.43,
          "en": "And that's therefore another awesome feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 212.43,
          "end": 215.25,
          "en": "that's unlocked by server components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 215.25,
          "end": 217.623,
          "en": "You can use them for data fetching.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}